---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import benchmarking from '../../assets/images/ux-benchmarking.png';
import journeyMap1 from '../../assets/images/journey-map-1.png';
---
<Layout title="Benchmarking | Andrew Smith" description="Quantitative UX benchmarking that measures the success of digital products over time — tracking effectiveness, efficiency, satisfaction, and desirability.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <div class="case-page">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main id="main-content">
      <section class="case-hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><a class="breadcrumb-link" href="/portfolio/work">Work</a><span class="breadcrumb-separator">/</span><span>Benchmarking</span></p>
        <h1 class="display-title">Measuring the success of digital products over time.</h1>
        <p class="hero-text">Shipping a feature is not the end of the design process — it is the start of the measurement phase. Benchmarking tracks whether a product is genuinely improving across four dimensions: effectiveness, efficiency, satisfaction, and desirability. Running the same study at regular intervals makes the data compound over time.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="meta-strip">
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Organisation</p><p class="meta-value">RAA</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Role</p><p class="meta-value">Senior UX Design Lead</p></div>
        <div class="meta-item"><p class="meta-label">Scope</p><p class="meta-value">Insurance, member portal, mobile app</p></div>
      </section>
      <section class="lead-image-section">
        <Image class="lead-image" src={benchmarking} alt="Usability benchmarking dashboard for insurance quote showing effectiveness 39/1, efficiency 4 minute average, satisfaction, and desirability word cloud" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
      <section class="summary-section">
        <p class="section-kicker">The Four Dimensions</p>
        <h2>Effectiveness, efficiency, satisfaction, and desirability.</h2>
        <div class="summary-main">
          <p>Effectiveness measures whether users completed the task. Efficiency measures how long it took. Satisfaction captures ease of use and perceived usefulness. Desirability captures the emotional quality of the experience through word-choice responses.</p>
          <p>Together these four dimensions give a complete picture of where the experience is working, where it is not, and what kind of problem each gap represents — which determines what kind of fix is needed.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="editorial-section">
        <div class="section-rail"><p class="section-kicker">Connecting to Journey Management</p></div>
        <div class="story-block">
          <p>Benchmarking data feeds directly into the journey map — adding quantitative metrics alongside the qualitative research findings. When win rates drop, drop-off rates climb, or desirability scores shift, the journey map captures those changes as evidence that a specific stage of the experience needs attention.</p>
          <p>This closes the loop between measurement and prioritisation. The data does not sit in a report — it informs what the team works on next.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="supporting-image-section">
        <Image class="supporting-image" src={journeyMap1} alt="QTB Journey Explorer showing live metrics connected to each stage of the member journey" loading="lazy" decoding="async" widths={[720,1080,1440]} sizes="(max-width:78rem) 100vw, 78rem"/>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
<style>
.case-page{position:relative;width:min(calc(100% - 3rem),78rem);margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 0 5rem}
.eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.82rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 1.25rem;display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}
.breadcrumb-link{font-weight:600}.breadcrumb-separator{color:var(--muted-foreground)}
h1,h2{margin:0;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.05em;color:var(--foreground)}
.display-title{font-size:clamp(2rem,4.5vw,3.5rem);line-height:1.06;margin:1rem 0 0;max-width:28ch}
.hero-text,.story-block p,.summary-main p{font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 1rem}
.case-hero{padding:5rem 0 2rem}
.meta-strip{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:2rem;padding:1.5rem 0 .5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}
.meta-label{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0}
.meta-value{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:1.1rem;font-weight:700}
.lead-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem}
.lead-image,.supporting-image{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1.5rem;box-shadow:var(--shadow-large)}
.supporting-image-section{padding:2rem 0 4rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section{padding:0 0 3rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.summary-section h2{margin-top:.75rem;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,2.5vw,2.2rem);max-width:32ch}
.summary-main{margin-top:1.5rem;max-width:44rem}
.section-kicker{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted-foreground);margin:0 0 .5rem}
.editorial-section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:14rem minmax(0,1fr);gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.story-block{max-width:44rem}
</style>
